1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Forty-Seventh Episode
The Battle of Vengeance
Wandering Franz

15
00:02:04,813 --> 00:02:05,491
Is that Little Coo?

16
00:02:05,515 --> 00:02:07,661
A letter from Prince Franz!

17
00:02:08,835 --> 00:02:10,615
Little Coo, thanks for your hard work.

18
00:02:10,639 --> 00:02:13,120
It's really hard work every day.

19
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:16,580
Both Sapphire and Franz sure love exchanging letters.

20
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,200
I see it, I see it!

21
00:02:24,413 --> 00:02:30,153
My beloved Princess Sapphire. To me, you are the moon, the stars, the sun.

22
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,693
Off you go!

23
00:02:57,130 --> 00:02:59,878
Those footsteps must be Prince Franz's.

24
00:02:59,902 --> 00:03:03,760
He gets so impatient whenever Princess Sapphire is concerned.

25
00:03:04,095 --> 00:03:05,980
Old Todd, is there a reply yet?

26
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:09,880
Please wait a little longer. It should arrive soon.

27
00:03:10,084 --> 00:03:12,573
Shall we play a game for old time's sake?

28
00:03:12,766 --> 00:03:13,553
Very well!

29
00:03:15,315 --> 00:03:16,626
Targeting both ends.

30
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,560
Five.

31
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,320
Five?

32
00:03:25,373 --> 00:03:26,160
Six.

33
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:30,720
I lost. I need another ten years of training.

34
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:32,751
Talking about your age again?

35
00:03:33,209 --> 00:03:34,233
Let's take a break.

36
00:03:36,313 --> 00:03:40,660
Oh, it's back! It's back! Prince Franz is eagerly waiting.

37
00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:46,986
What's the matter, Your Highness?

38
00:03:47,990 --> 00:03:50,160
It feels like a waste to open it right away.

39
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:56,666
Even a master swordsman loses his composure over Princess Sapphire.

40
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:01,520
Oh, this is from the Northern Fort.

41
00:04:02,715 --> 00:04:03,585
Prince Franz!

42
00:04:04,216 --> 00:04:05,673
Prince Franz!

43
00:04:08,930 --> 00:04:10,180
It's from the Northern Fort!

44
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:12,320
What? An unidentified fleet?

45
00:04:26,678 --> 00:04:27,505
Your Highness!

46
00:04:27,750 --> 00:04:29,060
There are so many of them!

47
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:32,940
It's the X-Union!

48
00:04:33,950 --> 00:04:35,170
Prince! Look out!

49
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,880
<i>To Prince Franz of Goldland...</i>

50
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:43,645
<i>Our X-Union is marching south with a million troops.</i>

51
00:04:43,669 --> 00:04:45,992
<i>Along the way, we subjugated those who surrendered</i>

52
00:04:46,016 --> 00:04:47,900
<i>and annihilated all who resisted.</i>

53
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:52,038
<i>Goldland, surrender without futile resistance.</i>

54
00:04:52,302 --> 00:04:56,760
<i>If we receive no answer by the time the moon sets in the west tonight, we will attack.
- The X-Union</i>

55
00:04:57,716 --> 00:04:59,966
Damn it! The X-Union again!

56
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:17,733
Looks like war is brewing. And a tough one, at that.

57
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:23,160
I thought I'd never wear that armor again, but I may have no choice.

58
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:28,220
Why must they bother attacking our peaceful Goldland?

59
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:36,740
That's the flag of Charcoalland. What could they want?

60
00:05:37,770 --> 00:05:41,060
What? The King of Charcoalland is sending us reinforcements?

61
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:42,272
Yes.

62
00:05:42,296 --> 00:05:46,184
He said he couldn't stand by during neighboring Goldland's crisis,

63
00:05:46,208 --> 00:05:47,657
and sent 50,000 troops...

64
00:05:47,682 --> 00:05:49,093
Oh, so many...

65
00:05:49,481 --> 00:05:52,112
Yes, they are already on standby at the border.

66
00:05:52,136 --> 00:05:55,266
With your permission, they can move immediately to defend Kamagishi...

67
00:05:56,714 --> 00:05:57,965
Wonderful, wonderful!

68
00:05:57,989 --> 00:06:00,385
Goldland has been saved from crisis.

69
00:06:00,409 --> 00:06:03,099
Make sure preparations are made for them to rest comfortably tonight...

70
00:06:15,930 --> 00:06:18,433
Halt! Stand by here!

71
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,611
Attention, all troops!

72
00:06:26,322 --> 00:06:28,400
The moon will soon sink behind the mountains!

73
00:06:29,035 --> 00:06:33,513
At the same time, the X-Union will undoubtedly attack from the north side of the inlet!

74
00:06:34,113 --> 00:06:34,658
However,

75
00:06:34,682 --> 00:06:38,405
King Charcoal next door is defending our eastern border.

76
00:06:38,429 --> 00:06:40,065
The real issue is this fortress.

77
00:06:40,089 --> 00:06:43,120
No matter how many enemies there are, we must hold this spot at all costs!

78
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:02,653
Battle stations!

79
00:07:15,110 --> 00:07:19,420
Pull back all forces and head for Goldland Castle! Follow me!

80
00:07:22,450 --> 00:07:26,000
It's begun... About time! Go, don't let them spot you!

81
00:07:53,893 --> 00:07:55,619
Charge!

82
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,780
The enemy has begun landing on the eastern shore.

83
00:08:03,804 --> 00:08:04,330
What!?

84
00:08:04,355 --> 00:08:07,072
50,000 Charcoal troops are supposed to be guarding the eastern shore...

85
00:08:07,096 --> 00:08:08,872
There's no one on the eastern shore.

86
00:08:08,896 --> 00:08:11,640
They say the Charcoal army headed for the castle earlier.

87
00:08:11,665 --> 00:08:12,486
What did you say!?

88
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:16,373
Were they drawn away...?

89
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:24,053
Quickly, it's dangerous here! Everyone, run!

90
00:08:24,860 --> 00:08:26,980
Head for Silverland!

91
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:30,672
To think there's a traitor among us...

92
00:08:30,696 --> 00:08:32,320
Either way, I can't just stand here!

93
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,260
Poor things...

94
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:59,440
What on earth happened?

95
00:08:59,945 --> 00:09:01,927
Has something happened in Goldland...?

96
00:09:27,669 --> 00:09:29,100
Have you seen Prince Franz?

97
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:31,680
Prince Franz is at the northern fortress.

98
00:09:32,020 --> 00:09:33,020
Thank you!

99
00:09:39,139 --> 00:09:40,180
It's the flag of Charcoalland!

100
00:09:40,230 --> 00:09:41,839
Suspicious fellow! Who are you?

101
00:09:42,025 --> 00:09:43,025
Ride on!

102
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:44,540
I'm counting on you!

103
00:09:47,467 --> 00:09:49,013
They're getting away!

104
00:09:50,981 --> 00:09:51,941
Halt!

105
00:09:59,939 --> 00:10:02,273
What? They're like the wind!

106
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,020
It's the Goldland soldiers!

107
00:10:15,849 --> 00:10:16,957
You might make it...

108
00:10:17,821 --> 00:10:18,666
Hang in there...

109
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:22,266
You've come to your senses, haven't you?

110
00:10:24,545 --> 00:10:25,545
W-Wait!

111
00:10:34,220 --> 00:10:37,730
I thought Prince Franz was the only swordsman better than me,

112
00:10:37,754 --> 00:10:40,266
but this Charcoal soldier is surprisingly skilled...

113
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:44,246
You are a worthy opponent! State your name!

114
00:10:44,990 --> 00:10:47,893
I... I am Silverland's Ribbon Knight!

115
00:10:48,674 --> 00:10:50,264
W-what? Then... That's right!

116
00:10:50,568 --> 00:10:51,944
I'm on your side!

117
00:10:52,194 --> 00:10:53,940
I came to help you!

118
00:10:54,345 --> 00:10:58,230
Oh dear, I am so terribly sorry...

119
00:10:58,388 --> 00:11:00,184
I'm just glad you understand.

120
00:11:00,221 --> 00:11:02,660
For a moment, I was worried sick about what would happen.

121
00:11:03,270 --> 00:11:07,240
I am deeply ashamed. I beg for your forgiveness, I beg of you!

122
00:11:08,593 --> 00:11:11,904
I was also trying to get to the northern fort,

123
00:11:11,928 --> 00:11:14,953
but I passed out when I got here.

124
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:19,110
Really, how pathetic of me. Come, lets go.

125
00:11:19,134 --> 00:11:20,446
I'm worried about Prince Franz.

126
00:11:21,449 --> 00:11:22,940
Then you're looking for Prince Franz too?

127
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:24,724
I'm the letter messenger between

128
00:11:24,749 --> 00:11:28,699
the prince and Princess Sapphire of your country.

129
00:11:29,170 --> 00:11:31,099
Then you're the one who always sends the pigeons?

130
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:34,980
So that's how it is. Alright, off I go!

131
00:11:45,409 --> 00:11:46,748
This is the end, Prince Franz!

132
00:11:46,772 --> 00:11:49,561
Goldland now belongs to the X-Union and me!

133
00:11:49,585 --> 00:11:51,546
Surrender already!

134
00:11:51,635 --> 00:11:53,228
Shut up, Charcoalland!

135
00:11:53,252 --> 00:11:56,146
This is the only answer a traitor like you deserves!

136
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,486
Crush them with sheer numbers!

137
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,540
Damn it! Am I too late?

138
00:12:29,901 --> 00:12:30,587
<i>Franz...</i>

139
00:13:05,699 --> 00:13:07,600
Franz! Prince Franz!

140
00:13:14,639 --> 00:13:15,980
Franz! Franz!

141
00:13:21,046 --> 00:13:23,020
Th-This is Prince Franz's...

142
00:13:58,836 --> 00:14:01,013
Hey, have you seen Prince Franz?

143
00:14:07,725 --> 00:14:09,460
No, no, I haven't seen him.

144
00:14:19,446 --> 00:14:20,066
<i>Franz...</i>

145
00:14:20,534 --> 00:14:21,541
<i>Please be alive.</i>

146
00:14:32,639 --> 00:14:34,020
Sapphire...

147
00:14:35,339 --> 00:14:40,580
Prince Franz, please come inside. The night dew is bad for your wounds.

148
00:14:40,673 --> 00:14:41,930
I know, my old friend.

149
00:14:42,147 --> 00:14:44,517
But I'm helpless like this.

150
00:14:45,114 --> 00:14:47,280
I can't walk, and we have no horses.

151
00:14:48,459 --> 00:14:50,400
And Goldland Castle is in that state as well.

152
00:14:51,439 --> 00:14:53,460
I understand how you feel.

153
00:14:55,329 --> 00:14:56,477
But Your Highness,

154
00:14:56,961 --> 00:15:02,093
once you heal, you can retake the castle anytime.

155
00:15:02,865 --> 00:15:05,553
Come, let us treat your wounds.

156
00:15:13,119 --> 00:15:16,800
<i>Prince! Please, let Franz be safe!</i>

157
00:15:26,949 --> 00:15:30,379
Your Highness, please write a letter to Princess Sapphire.

158
00:15:31,340 --> 00:15:32,752
But how will we deliver it?

159
00:15:32,776 --> 00:15:35,785
These two legs of mine will be the pigeon!

160
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:36,625
But...

161
00:15:36,649 --> 00:15:39,205
The Princess must be worried about you.

162
00:15:39,229 --> 00:15:41,012
Come, take off your cloak,

163
00:15:41,036 --> 00:15:41,705
On this...?

164
00:15:41,823 --> 00:15:45,313
spread it out, and write on it with this ink pen!

165
00:15:45,625 --> 00:15:46,992
Hurry!

166
00:15:47,549 --> 00:15:49,240
That's a great idea!

167
00:15:51,139 --> 00:15:55,652
Besides, our soldiers must have escaped to Silverland.

168
00:15:55,676 --> 00:15:58,920
Your Highness, We must let them know that you are safe.

169
00:16:06,609 --> 00:16:09,624
Well then, I shall return by noon tomorrow.

170
00:16:09,648 --> 00:16:10,580
Farewell.

171
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,780
Hey, this one's a big catch.

172
00:16:13,846 --> 00:16:16,266
Capturing them will be a major triumph!

173
00:16:16,985 --> 00:16:19,731
All right, leave the helpless prince for later.

174
00:16:19,755 --> 00:16:21,920
First, let's take care of that old geezer!

175
00:16:35,689 --> 00:16:37,260
We should catch up to him soon!

176
00:16:43,660 --> 00:16:45,620
You old fool!

177
00:16:46,322 --> 00:16:47,682
Help me!

178
00:16:49,104 --> 00:16:51,546
I won't just let you escape!

179
00:16:53,919 --> 00:16:54,940
Goldland soldiers!

180
00:16:55,259 --> 00:16:56,259
Come on then!

181
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:00,226
Halt! Seize him!

182
00:17:04,622 --> 00:17:05,608
Hyah!

183
00:17:14,369 --> 00:17:17,833
Don't let him escape! Whatever you do, don't let him reach Silverland!

184
00:17:24,034 --> 00:17:25,526
Easy there, old man!

185
00:17:25,889 --> 00:17:27,380
Oh, Ribbon Knight!

186
00:17:27,593 --> 00:17:28,620
It's Ribbon!

187
00:17:28,849 --> 00:17:31,553
Come on, Silverland is just ahead! Follow me!

188
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,360
Where did they go?!

189
00:17:34,539 --> 00:17:36,926
Get them!

190
00:17:44,479 --> 00:17:46,860
So they've finally fled into Silverland!

191
00:17:46,884 --> 00:17:47,833
Damn it!

192
00:17:49,319 --> 00:17:50,520
Hang in there! We're almost there, old man!

193
00:17:51,699 --> 00:17:53,820
Hey! Somebody open up!

194
00:17:55,429 --> 00:17:56,520
W-What happened?

195
00:17:57,279 --> 00:17:59,260
Prince Franz is safe.

196
00:18:00,479 --> 00:18:04,280
He's wounded and hiding in Shinewood Cave.

197
00:18:04,539 --> 00:18:06,020
Then we must go there at once!

198
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,180
Hurry, quickly!

199
00:18:08,599 --> 00:18:13,160
Ribbon Knight, please deliver this to Lady Sapphire in my place.

200
00:18:14,719 --> 00:18:16,293
Is this Prince Franz's cloak?

201
00:18:17,019 --> 00:18:19,984
That's a letter from the prince to Princess Sapphire.

202
00:18:20,008 --> 00:18:22,684
Ah, hey now, you shouldn't read someone else's mail!

203
00:18:22,708 --> 00:18:24,520
My goodness...

204
00:18:24,969 --> 00:18:28,318
Thank you for everything, Princess Knight.

205
00:18:28,342 --> 00:18:30,331
But my only regret is...

206
00:18:30,355 --> 00:18:31,711
Your regret?

207
00:18:31,735 --> 00:18:36,720
I wanted to deliver Lord Franz's letter directly to Princess Sapphire myself.

208
00:18:37,419 --> 00:18:39,460
That's the only pity.

209
00:18:48,619 --> 00:18:51,320
I just wanted to see Princess Sapphire.

210
00:18:51,835 --> 00:18:52,835
Old Todd!

211
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:54,619
Old Todd!

212
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:55,980
Who are you?

213
00:18:56,999 --> 00:19:01,940
I'm Sapphire. Thank you for all your letters, Old Todd.

214
00:19:03,719 --> 00:19:08,800
She is every bit as kind a princess as I thought.

215
00:19:12,413 --> 00:19:14,458
My duty is finally fulfilled.

216
00:19:14,488 --> 00:19:18,171
Princess Sapphire, please look after Prince Franz.

217
00:19:18,195 --> 00:19:22,993
Join forces and defeat those villains!

218
00:19:23,899 --> 00:19:26,380
Yes, Old Todd. Always.

219
00:19:26,929 --> 00:19:31,920
Wonderful. I can rest easy now.

220
00:19:33,243 --> 00:19:34,531
Old Todd!

221
00:19:35,728 --> 00:19:36,886
Old Todd!

222
00:19:43,609 --> 00:19:44,700
Come on, let's go!

223
00:19:57,929 --> 00:19:59,391
<i>Dearest Sapphire,</i>

224
00:19:59,415 --> 00:20:02,604
<i>Goldland is now overrun with enemy troops. </i>

225
00:20:02,628 --> 00:20:05,173
<i>My leg is injured and I cannot move.</i>

226
00:20:08,689 --> 00:20:11,178
<i>I may never see you alive again,</i>

227
00:20:11,642 --> 00:20:16,273
<i>but I'm truly happy to have met you in this world.</i>

228
00:20:18,909 --> 00:20:21,264
<i>I am prepared to fight bravely to the end,</i>

229
00:20:21,288 --> 00:20:23,260
<i>as a prince of Goldland should.</i>

230
00:20:25,379 --> 00:20:29,340
<i>Even if I should fall, my heart will always be by your side.</i>

231
00:20:30,399 --> 00:20:35,120
<i>I sincerely pray for your happiness. To Sapphire, from Prince Franz.</i>

232
00:20:50,799 --> 00:20:52,080
Franz! Don't die!

233
00:20:57,129 --> 00:20:58,853
Prince Franz! Are you safe?

234
00:21:01,464 --> 00:21:02,860
Oh, the Ribbon Knight!

235
00:21:08,580 --> 00:21:09,580
Prince Franz!

236
00:21:12,469 --> 00:21:15,360
It looks like a new unit of enemy troops has arrived. For now...

237
00:21:15,384 --> 00:21:18,113
Come on, everyone! We're pulling back!

238
00:21:28,379 --> 00:21:30,920
Princess Sapphire is waiting at that farmhouse.

239
00:21:31,910 --> 00:21:33,040
Here, I'm returning this to you.

240
00:21:35,729 --> 00:21:37,253
How did the Ribbon Knight have this?

241
00:21:58,020 --> 00:22:02,153
Old friend, I swear we will take Goldland back with our own hands!

242
00:22:07,549 --> 00:22:10,960
Old friend, I promise I will honor your friendship!

243
00:22:13,689 --> 00:22:17,483
And at the very end, the old man said that Goldland and Silverland...

244
00:22:17,507 --> 00:22:20,960
should join hands and defeat the enemy...

245
00:22:26,449 --> 00:22:33,960
<i>Please look after Prince Franz. And may you both be happy forever...</i>

246
00:22:37,799 --> 00:22:43,933
Old Todd prayed that you would stay strong and find happiness, Franz.

247
00:22:45,364 --> 00:22:48,020
Thank you, Sapphire. I won't lose heart ever again.

248
00:22:50,829 --> 00:22:54,860
And I'll make sure to move his grave back to Goldland Castle.

249
00:22:56,499 --> 00:23:01,980
I'll put an end to this war and restore peace to Goldland once and for all.

250
00:23:02,919 --> 00:23:05,000
Will you help me, Sapphire?

251
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:18,960
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

252
00:24:18,961 --> 00:24:22,321
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

253
00:24:22,322 --> 00:24:26,092
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

254
00:24:26,093 --> 00:24:29,254
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

255
00:24:29,255 --> 00:24:33,068
♪ Sen'nen man'nen hyakuman-nen ♪
A thousand years, ten thousand years, a million years,

